 "notes": "Endpoints: the committed swagger (docs/spec.json, no basePath) plus the routes that exist only in the code (GET /swagger, /docs, /mcp via g.Match, and the UI files in ui/serve.go). Scope: router/ and ui/serve.go. Misses: GET /version and /gotifyinfo are registered on the gin engine without a leading slash (no-leading-slash: relative patterns are only accepted on groups); POST /user is registered on a group created in the same chained expression, g.Group(\"/user\").Use(mw).POST(\"\", h) (group-chain); GET / in ui/serve.go hangs from a group of the router passed in (router-as-param). The example plugin route (plugin/example/echo) is mounted under /plugin/{id}/custom/{token}/ by the plugin manager (router-as-param). Calls: every axios call of the React UI (ui/src, tests excluded), as written after the configured base URL. Eight are dropped because the first segment is a MIME type head — application/{id}, message — which looks_like_rel_path takes for application/json (mime-like-head); one goes through axios.create().request({url, method}) (request-config-object). Since the v2 cheap fixes (2026-10-15): the group prefix is carried through the chain and application/{id}, message are paths. Three calls written with the receiver on the line above (axios\\n.delete(...)) were missing from this list — the listing grep had the extractor's blind spot — and were added: DELETE /client/{id}, DELETE /user/{id}, POST /current/user/password. axios.put(url, app) is still dropped: a variable named app as the second argument looks like a handler (data-taken-for-handler). Since 2026-10-17 axios.create().request({ url: config.get('url') + 'auth/local/login', method: 'POST' }) is read (a request described by an object). Since F1.14 increment 3 (2026-10-18) the verbs of Match are read, and HEAD /health — g.Match([]string{\"GET\", \"HEAD\"}, \"/health\", ...), outside the swagger — was added.",
